            "params": {
              "text": "<p><strong>Welcome to Module 13: Supporting Social and Emotional Well-being in Young Children.</strong></p><hr><p>The purpose of this module on Social and Emotional Well-Being in Young Children is to provide Early Childhood Education teachers with practical, job-embedded professional opportunities to learn about the importance of 3 to 4-year-old children’s development of social and emotional skills for present well-being, plus future school and lifelong success. Participants will learn evidence-based practices to enhance children’s social and emotional development.&nbsp; The Module is comprised of four interactive, synchronous sessions, two associated asynchronous learning activities, and two products that are designed to assist participants with their daily practice. These practical, job-embedded activities and products will enable participants to apply the new knowledge and skills that they are learning in the Module in their work contexts.&nbsp;</p><p>Go <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://new-moodle.oecs.org/course/view.php?id=96&amp;section=1\">HERE</a> to learn more.</p>"
            },
            "library": "H5P.Text 1.1",
            "metadata": {
